The "Payment Collapse" Paradox: A defining characteristic of the current landscape is the plummeting rate of ransom payments. Only 28% of victims chose to pay ransoms, marking an all-time low
. In response, threat actors are aggressively shifting toward "pure extortion" or "data-theft first" models, prioritizing the public exposure of sensitive data over simply encrypting systems
. However, for those who do pay, the median ransom payment has surged 368% to $59,556
.

